      "full_assistant_content_exact": "Based on the information provided, here is the solution:\n\n1.  **Analyze the Wall**: The problem states that a wall is built around a square area using 36 identical cubes. The image shows that the wall is 1 cube thick.\n\n2.  **Determine the Square's Dimensions**: Let the side length of the square area be $n$ (in cubes). The perimeter of a square is given by $P = 4 \\times \\text{side length}$.\n    Since the wall is 1 cube thick and wraps around the outside, the total number of cubes used for the wall corresponds to the perimeter.\n    $$36 = 4 \\times n$$\n    $$n = \\frac{36}{4}$$\n    $$n = 9$$\n    So, the side of the square area is 9 cubes long.\n\n3.  **Calculate the Fill**: To find how many cubes are needed to completely fill the square area, calculate the area of the square ($n \\times n$).\n    $$\\text{Total cubes} = 9 \\times 9 = 81$$\n\n**Answer:**\n**81** cubes are needed to completely fill the square area.",
